  "spiritual_reading": "# The Five Liberations of Wisdom from the Dominion of Falsity\n\n---\n\n** ¶1:** There are five stages of liberation by which wisdom is recovered from all the dominions and governing powers of falsity and evil.\n\n**¶2:** The first loos ening and recovery is that of the celest ial mind itself. For when the primordial divine understanding was delivered from its captivity under the rule of falsities by the proceeding divine life— which had come forth toward it — an immense measure of wisdom and spiritual power was recovered from the entire government of evil. These asc ended together with the celestial mind into the heavenly degrees of the Lord 's kingdom . This is the first liberation.\n\n**¶3:** The second recovery is that accomplished through the proceeding divine life. For when Divine Love and Divine Wisdom together formed the interior degrees and the exterior natural states of the mind—and brought order to the natural states and the false persu asions ruling within them —an immeas urable portion of wisdom was recovered from these : all that the celest ial mind had yiel ded up when it was consumed by the assault of falsity…\n\n**¶4:** *( The text is largely lost here.) * … through three states of spiritual combat… extending to the time when… above … them upon… the whole order of the mind.\n\n** ¶5:** The third recovery is that of the Divine Truth proceeding further into the rational degree. It made visible the form of heavenly wisdom… before the governing power of falsity… and recovered wisdom from it. This, then , is how the form of divine truth is made manifest through this further proceeding into the lower understanding .\n\n**¶6:** The fourth recovery is that of Divine Truth itself revealed in its full splendor. For when it was made manifest within the sphere of spiritual life, it displayed the form of heavenly wisdom before the fixed structures of the understanding and purified all the wisdom dwelling in the higher degrees. It brought order to the natural states of mind and all the bonds and attach ments holding them in place. It also released wisdom beyond measure throughout the entire structure of the regener ating mind. It gave the calling - forth of truth and the capacity of willing reception to the fundamental faculties, and from these it formed a new interior will— a new love of good born within truth . It then ascended and came to rest in the celestial state.\n\n** ¶7:** The fifth liberation and recovery is that of divine providence working as a whole — which is the calling- forth of truth and the responsive reception by the will—since this, too, recovers the interior spiritual life from out of the heav enly degrees and carries it into its final embod iment.\n\n**¶8:** *(Much is lost.) * …the proceeding divine life… as it accomplished each liberation… The first… ascended… wisdom… The fourth… its wisdom… And also the fifth… enters into the whole and brings all into final order… the form of wisdom made visible in this ultimate containing vessel—the Last Form in which all recovered good is gathered and embodied.\n\n**¶9 :** These five great powers of liberation were made manifest . They came to their increase and fruition; they were established upon the foundation of… the celestial mind… when it came forth from spiritual combat. It brought order to and built up the whole structure of the mind… the celestial mind… through its advent into the world.\n\n**¶10 :** In this way they stand together in their ordering …\n\n**¶11:** … because of the wisdom that had rushed forth from… the proceeding Divine Truth in the rational degree.\n\n**¶12:** The governance of divine providence—which is the calling -forth of truth and its reception by the will—shall accomplish its final work. In this last state of spiritual development, it shall bring life to the ultimate Form, and that Form shall judge all interior spiritual states and shall send forth its powers. It is alive according to the will of the Divine Father, the One who is established and all -powerful. They go forth against evil; they overcome all of it ; they conquer the natural mind in which they had lab ored forever . For they came forth from Him in the beginning , even as they shall return again into wisdom. They ascend to Him at the last.",
  "reconstructions": [
    {
      "paragraph": 1,
      "reconstructed_text": "[There are] five [releases by] which the light is saved f[rom] all [the rulers and] powers of darkness!"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 2,
      "reconstructed_text": "[The first loo]sening and saving is that of [the] First Man, since when the First M[a]n was freed fro[m the prison of] the rulers by the Living Spirit, who had come [forth to the aid] of the First Man, much light and [much] power was saved from the entire ruling-power. They ascended with the First Man to the aeons [of] greatn[ess]. This [is the first] release."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 3,
      "reconstructed_text": "The second saving is that of the Liv[ing] Spirit, since whe[n] the Father of Life and [the] Mother of [Li]fe constructed [the heavens] and [w]orlds [and set in order the wo]rlds, the earths and their [rulers; im]measurable light was saved f[r]om them [, all that the First] Man, who w[a]s devoured [by the darkness, had lost of his] lig[ht and power.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 4,
      "reconstructed_text": "[And there were] [also] three wars [that were waged,] to the time when he [was raised up] above [all of] them upon the [whole] universe."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 6,
      "reconstructed_text": "[Th]e fourth s[av]ing is that of Jesus the Splendour, since whe[n he was] re[ve]aled in the zone he displayed [his im]age in front of the firmaments and purified [the light] that is above. He took the likeness [of the powers, and] he made himself like the angels in [every aeon,] un[til] he travelled and descended to the form of flesh. He set in order [t]he earths and all the fastenings. He also loosen[ed and saved] light without measure in the entire structure. He gave [the] summons and the obedience to the elements, he formed [J]esus the Youth. He as[ce]n[d]ed and rested himself in the light [land]."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 7,
      "reconstructed_text": "The fifth release and saving is that of the great counsel, w[hich is the s]umm[ons an]d the obedience, since it also [sends forth] the soul from the [land] of greatness."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 8,
      "reconstructed_text": "[And] the Living Spirit [accomplished his work,] as he gave [forth] the release [of the light in each.] The first [power rose; he] ascended and he [saved the light,] as he [brought forth] wisdom [from the darkness.] The fourth [also brought forth] its wisdom [in like manner.] And also, the fifth [enters] into it, and it sets it in order [and manifests] its light image in this Last Statue."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 10,
      "reconstructed_text": "In [t]his way [also] they st[an]d with [one another in their ordering.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 11,
      "reconstructed_text": "[And this is] because of the light [th]at had rushed from [the image of] the Amba[s]sa[d]or."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 5,
      "reconstructed_text": "[The third red]emption is that of the Thi[rd Ambassador, since when he] displayed [his image before the firmaments, and] he [purified the light from the r]uling-power; he [loosened and saved light] from them [without measure.] So this is [how] the [form of] his image that [is revealed] in the Th[ir]d Ambassador."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 9,
      "reconstructed_text": "These five grea[t] powe[rs of saving] were revealed. They came to a profit [and a gain;] they were established upon [the foundation of the] First Man [himself,] when he came to/ward [the light] from the struggle. He set in order and constructed [the] universe [through] the First M[an at] his advent."
    }
  ],
